 "par": {
  "time": 480
 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "THE RELIQUARY ROAD",
  "lines": [
   "The road to the Deep is lined with graves.",
   "Every one of them is from somewhere else."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Next: the Chitin Aqueduct. The only water on the world that still moves.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [11, 11],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A road lined with graves. Not mounds: slabs stood on end with a bronze band across them, in rows. Somebody sweeps them. The bronze is bright."
  },
  {
   "id": "arches",
   "at": [18, 11],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The roofed arches have walls: nothing shoots down into them. The open stretches between are the long shots. The wall panels beside you will open."
  },
  {
   "id": "tools",
   "at": [15, 5],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Hand tools, a whole chapel of them: planes, saws, chisels, one pattern, thousands, hung in rows. They made everything with the same few things."
  },
  {
   "id": "clocks",
   "at": [33, 5],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A clock on every grave, and no two agree. Somebody wound them all, once. Nobody has since."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate1",
   "at": [48, 11],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: one number, 211,408, and a short falling note. The same number is on the slab beside it, and the one beside that."
  },
  {
   "id": "boots",
   "at": [61, 22],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Boots in pairs, a pair to a grave, laced. The pairs go small, large, small."
  },
  {
   "id": "lamps",
   "at": [33, 26],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Lamps: brass, glass, clay, a hundred ways of holding a flame. They liked to see what they were doing."
  },
  {
   "id": "nets",
   "at": [19, 28],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Nets, folded, a net to a grave, folded the way you fold one you mean to use again."
  },
  {
   "id": "grate",
   "at": [6, 36],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A grate in the west wall, bolted on this side. Behind it a stair climbs back up to the tools chapel at the head of the road."
  },
  {
   "id": "strings",
   "at": [29, 41],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Stringed instruments, one to a grave, and every string cut."
  },
  {
   "id": "split",
   "at": [30, 43],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The back wall of this chapel is cracked through, and the cracks are clean. Something is kept behind it. A shot would open it."
  },
  {
   "id": "kept",
   "at": [30, 47],
   "radius": 1.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A reliquary. Harpoon bolts packed in frost, laid out like a saint's bones, and a vest for whoever came to take them."
  },
  {
   "id": "end",
   "at": [53, 37],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The road ends in a yard of bare slabs, with a door in the far wall and a shell-back in front of it. Two sextons with it. Everything here that can be raised, they'll raise."
  },
  {
   "id": "bare",
   "at": [40, 49],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Rows of bare slabs, the bronze polished, nothing laid on them yet. A great many. These are new. There's a lever on the west wall."
  },
  {
   "id": "name",
   "at": [63, 46],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A bare slab with a name cut in our letters. Calder. There is no bronze on it yet. I am not going to look for a date."
  },
  {
   "id": "lever",
   "at": [0, 0],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The lever works a bar across the door at the end of the road. Somewhere ahead, iron lifts."
  },
  {
   "id": "open",
   "at": [0, 0],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The door at the end of the road is open."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [59, 46],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The east wall of this yard rings hollow."
  },
  {
   "id": "keyhunt",
   "at": [19, 37],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A reliquary key, worn thin by people who carried it for luck."
  }
 ],
 "objective": "Follow the road down the hill. The exit is locked: a lever in the chapel of bare slabs at the foot, and a guard",
